  "behavior": [
    "The original e724364 Rust source reproduced a real defect: expire a protected task callback, restart the server with the same database and authenticated native task grant, reopen the old session, and an ordinary provider call was dispatched.",
    "Schema 16 stores an immutable session-to-original-setup binding before process-local registration. The binding holds a credential reference and bounded grant definition; nonce uniqueness prevents one private invocation being installed on two sessions. No bearer, callback secret, private path or provider body is added to this table.",
    "Admission revalidates current task/credential/caller/route and exact stored setup identity before the existing one-time physical dispatch. Competing registrations yield one winner; different-nonce replacement and cross-session nonce reuse fail without mutation. Storage failure rolls back and permits an exact known-unsent retry.",
    "After expiry and actual server restart, native and owner media attachment cannot fall back or replace the original setup. The original private intent is unchanged. A new session on the same task/conversation attaches tools, retains the old context source and exchanges actual QUIC audio with the local fake Vapi bridge.",
    "Voice-only task sessions without a configured tool setup retain their existing call/audio behavior. The full scoped-history and post-call-context regression passes, as do cancellation, concurrent calls, pending continuation, revocation and uncertain-call reconciliation.",
    "Expired and ended setup entries are removed from memory after listener shutdown. The immutable Store binding remains. Shared 32-listener capacity, expiry, shutdown closure and zero provider calls during idle setup qualification pass.",
    "Backup-gated migration preserves existing state and reserves older task-linked sessions with unknown setup identity; it never invents an old nonce. Those legs require a new session on the existing task/conversation. Matching snapshot digests cover new binding rows; rollback and original-schema backup preservation are tested."
  ],
